  "reason": "No disclosed ordinary explanation for the FY22 PAT spike (2.1x vs FY20‑21 average) in the provided RHP pages. The financials (rhp:p45, p154) show revenue grew 46.5% YoY but employee costs jumped 87% and other expenses 92%; the margin improvement stems largely from a large inventory build‑up (change in inventories ‑₹3.75 cr vs ‑₹0.58 cr) and lower finance costs, not from an order book, capex plan, or one‑off gain. The results discussion (rhp:p198) covers only the nine months ended Dec‑22, not FY22 vs prior years. The business description (rhp:p108) provides no narrative justification.",
